			"notes": "Fixes interrupted or jumping unequip animation when a presentation moves between the current-item and outgoing-item channels.\n\nThe client now retains each protocol session's animation clock, transition, spring state and last viewport sample across channel moves and reclamation. Two profiles using the same model asset receive independent playback while sharing reference-counted uploaded textures. Clearing a channel still removes it immediately; only a subsequent ownership frame restores that session as an outgoing or reclaimed presentation. Options are applied with their following ownership frame, and superseded uploads cannot overwrite an already resolved presentation.\n\n- Builds for Minecraft 1.21.8, 1.21.9, 1.21.10, 1.21.11, 26.1, 26.1.1, 26.1.2 and 26.2.\n- Protocol remains 9. No plugin update is required for this fix.\n- Includes the Sodium armor fix from 0.9.1-preview.\n- Install only the runtime JAR matching your exact Minecraft version. Source JARs are excluded from release assets.\n\nValidation: clean builds, headless tests, exact-version mixin bytecode checks and gametest-source compilation for all eight targets. Regression coverage compares migrated and uninterrupted animation at 30, 60, 144 and 240 FPS, exercises rapid same-asset profile changes and reclamation, checks shared texture lifetime and stale uploads, and checks legacy generic/rifle unequip plus modern raygun reverse-equip fixtures. Connected-client visual validation was not performed."
		},
