			"notes": "Fixes Armature armor appearing tiny or misplaced when Sodium is installed.\n\nArmor now emits its authored body-local mesh through Minecraft's equipment renderer. It no longer replaces the polygons of a temporary one-pixel cube, whose constructor geometry Sodium caches. This preserves the model's dimensions, bone transforms, rotated legacy faces and atlas UVs while keeping Minecraft's equipment textures, dyes, trims and glint.\n\n- Builds for Minecraft 1.21.8, 1.21.9, 1.21.10, 1.21.11, 26.1, 26.1.1, 26.1.2 and 26.2.\n- Protocol remains 9; no plugin update is required for this fix.\n- Install only the runtime JAR matching your exact Minecraft version. Source JARs are excluded from release assets.\n\nValidation: 71 headless tests passed for each of the eight targets, including equipment vertex/UV/color/lighting checks and exact-version mixin bytecode checks. The new regression test fails against the previous armor implementation. Gametest sources compiled for all targets; connected-client visual validation with Sodium/Iris was not performed."
		},
