			"notes": "Adds version-specific Fabric builds for Minecraft **1.21.8, 1.21.9, 1.21.10, 1.21.11, 26.1, 26.1.1, 26.1.2 and 26.2**.\n\nDownload **one runtime JAR matching your exact Minecraft version**. Source code is available from the repository and GitHub's automatic source archives.\n\n| Minecraft | Java | Optional Mod Menu |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1.21.8 | 21+ | 15.x |\n| 1.21.9 / 1.21.10 | 21+ | 16.x |\n| 1.21.11 | 21+ | 17.x |\n| 26.1 / 26.1.1 / 26.1.2 | 25+ | 18.x |\n| 26.2 | 25+ | 20.x |\n\nFabric Loader 0.19.5+ and Fabric API for the selected Minecraft version are required. Client protocol remains **9**; use a compatible Armature server plugin.\n\nThe port adapts hand/model submission, armor and held-item rendering, movement interpolation, camera/projection hooks, networking and the Mod Menu screen. Authored animation and profile behavior stays shared, including legacy models, bone scale, neutral held-item conditions and server-renderer handoff. Minecraft 26.2 uses native rendering abstractions with no raw OpenGL calls.\n\n**Validation:** 69 headless tests pass per target, including every configured mixin's signatures against that exact Minecraft JAR. Interactive client tests compile for all eight versions. The standalone source export also compiles independently.\n\n**Preview:** connected-client visual tests, Iris shaderpack behavior and Vulkan rendering still need in-game verification. No Minecraft client or server was launched for this release.\n\nSee the [README](https://github.com/Cryxow/ArmatureClientMod#readme) for installation, exact Fabric API versions and build instructions. SHA256SUMS.txt lists the hashes of the attached JARs. Source is MIT licensed and can be forked or integrated into a server-specific client mod."
