			"notes": "First public standalone release of Armature Client Mod.\n\n## Install\n\n- Minecraft **1.21.8**, Fabric Loader **0.19.5+**, Java **21+**.\n- Install Fabric API for 1.21.8; Mod Menu **15.x** is optional.\n- Put **armature-client-fabric-1.21.8-0.8.5-preview.jar** in your instance's `mods` folder.\n- Source code is available from the repository and GitHub's automatic source archives.\n- Your server needs a compatible Armature plugin using **protocol 9**, with the native backend and client rendering enabled. Protocol 8 plugins need updating before using this release.\n\n## Open-source distribution\n\nThe mod is MIT licensed and can be used, modified, forked and integrated into server-specific client mods. Preserve the license and copyright notice. The source repository builds independently from the plugin and includes the exact shared Armature samplers/protocol used by this release.\n\n- [Installation and build](https://github.com/Cryxow/ArmatureClientMod#readme)\n- [Integrating into another Fabric mod](https://github.com/Cryxow/ArmatureClientMod/blob/main/docs/INTEGRATION.md)\n- [Protocol contract](https://github.com/Cryxow/ArmatureClientMod/blob/main/docs/PROTOCOL.md)\n- [Contributing](https://github.com/Cryxow/ArmatureClientMod/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n\n## Validation\n\nStandalone build, **68 headless tests**, client gametest compilation and GitHub build/release workflows passed. Minecraft/server gametests were not launched for this release; shaderpack and connected-client visual compatibility remain preview features requiring in-game verification."
